      "title": "Australian politics live: Liberal MP ‘reached out’ to Anne Aly after saying she should be ‘shamed and stoned’; Nationals condemn ‘risky’ pineapples",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/oct/14/treasurer-jim-chalmers-labor-one-nation-pauline-hanson-one-nation-gas-reservation-scheme-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Follow the day’s news live.</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p><strong>Australia missing out on $45bn of revenue from resources: Greens</strong></p><p>As Labor prepares to introduce its bill for a gas reserve, the Greens are pointing out that there are tens of billions being left on the table because the government won’t properly tax the resource.</p><p>We’re giving away billions in resource wealth while families struggle to pay the rent, put food on the table and afford basic healthcare.</p><p>Labor can find billions to prop up the fossil fuel industry, but when it comes to making corporations like Santos, Woodside and Adani pay a fair return, suddenly it’s all too hard.</p><p>The prime minister has a kink for punishing small businesses and a fetish for humiliating his treasurer. So I say this is a consistent pattern of behaviour where the prime minister constantly goes in, overrides his treasurer, humiliates him in public. I suspect it’s going to sour the relationship somewhat.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/oct/14/treasurer-jim-chalmers-labor-one-nation-pauline-hanson-one-nation-gas-reservation-scheme-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-14T02:22:46"
    },
