      "title": "Rachel Smith will turn 39 in prison. The high court says she could freeze her eggs from behind bars",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/14/rachel-smith-will-turn-39-in-prison-the-high-court-says-she-could-freeze-her-eggs-from-behind-bars",
      "description": "<p>Australia’s highest court says Queensland drug trafficker extracting and storing eggs is not ‘assisted reproductive technology’</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>A woman has won an appeal in Australia’s highest court about her right to freeze her eggs while behind bars.</p><p>Rachel Smith is serving a 10-year prison term in <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/queensland\">Queensland</a> for trafficking in a dangerous drug.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/14/rachel-smith-will-turn-39-in-prison-the-high-court-says-she-could-freeze-her-eggs-from-behind-bars\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-14T01:45:13"
    },
